# core §1 — BARE MEANS NO QUOTE ANYWHERE IN THE TOKEN.
#
# Every line below parsed until this release: a token quoted only in part
# had its quotes silently removed, so `node a"b"` declared the id `ab` and
# `"node" x` was `node x`. Each is now the error a wholly quoted token in
# the same position gets. The header's own case (`figdown 0".5" block`)
# cannot share a file with these; the property test in run.js covers it.
figdown 0.5 block
node a"b"
node "c"d
"node" x
no"de" y
flow r"ight"
node ok "OK"
